              "h94TQOK7NRA@3033",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3046",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3047",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3050",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3052",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3054"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch03.s08.p06.r04",
            "text": "Printing the context vectors shows that the first 6 × 2 matrix corresponds to the first input and the second 6 × 2 matrix corresponds to the second input, stacked together.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3058",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3061",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3064",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3067",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3069",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3071",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3074",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3076",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3078",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3079"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch03.s08.p06.r05",
            "text": "That confirms that the implemented causal attention class can handle batches.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3082",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3084",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3086"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch03.s08.p07",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch03.s08.p07.01",
            "text": "A few implementation details make this class easier to use correctly.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch03.s08.p07.02",
            "text": "A buffer is useful for fixed tensors such as the causal mask that do not need to be trained.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3088",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3089",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3092",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3112",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3114",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3117",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3123"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch03.s08.p07.03",
            "text": "Using \"register_buffer\" for fixed matrices like the mask causes them to move automatically with the model to the appropriate device, such as CPU or GPU.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3100",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3101",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3103",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3105",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3125",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3127",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3131",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3133",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3162",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3163"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch03.s08.p07.04",
            "text": "Defining fixed, untrained tensors with \"register_buffer\" is more convenient because it avoids manually ensuring that they are on the same device as the model parameters and helps prevent device mismatch errors.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3134",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3137",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3140",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3142",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3144",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3146",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3157",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3159",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3163",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3166",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3167",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3169"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch03.s08.p07.05",
            "text": "Slicing the mask by the number of tokens ensures that if a batch has fewer tokens than the supported context size, the mask is created only up to the actual number of tokens.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3171",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3173",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3177",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3179",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3181",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3183",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3188",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3190",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3192"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch03.s08.p07.06",
            "text": "Taken together, this class applies a causal attention mask so that elements above the diagonal are set to zero, uses softmax so each row of attention weights sums to one, and includes dropout for generalizability and to prevent overfitting.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3206",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3208",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3211",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3213",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3215",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3218",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3219",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3222",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3224",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3227"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch03.s08.p07.07",
            "text": "Stacking multiple causal attention heads together leads to multi-head attention, which is what GPT implements.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3236",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3238",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3240",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3247",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3250",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3252",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3265",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3267",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3269",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3270",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3272"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch03.s08.p07.08",
            "text": "To understand multi-head attention, it is necessary first to understand causal attention, and causal attention in turn depends on understanding keys, queries, and values.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3277",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3278",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3281",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3283",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3285",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3287"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch03.s08.p07.09",
            "text": "Understanding dimensions, batches, three-dimensional tensors, matrices, and linear algebra fundamentals is therefore important for understanding how attention works.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3313",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3315",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3317",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3319",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3322",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3323",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3325",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3327",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3330",
              "h94TQOK7NRA@3331"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
